-- title:
--   Uniform lower bound for the chordal pair height
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with an algebra structure over $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $r$ be a natural number and let $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to F$ be a family of $r$ elements of $F$. Here a place of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, in the sense of `Place (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F`, is a valuation subring of $F$ that contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring; attached to $s$ and such a place $v$ is the evaluation vector `evalVec s v` $\in \overline{\mathbb Q}^{\,r}$. For a finite family $x$ of algebraic numbers, $\mathrm{absLogHeight}(x)$ denotes the logarithmic height of $x$ computed in the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by its entries, divided by the degree over $\mathbb Q$ of that subfield; the chord vector $\mathrm{chordVec}\,s\,v\,w$ is the family of $2\times 2$ minors $\bigl(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v\bigr)_i\bigl(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,w\bigr)_j - \bigl(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v\bigr)_j\bigl(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,w\bigr)_i$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,r \times \mathrm{Fin}\,r$, and the pair height is $\mathrm{pairHt}\,s\,v\,w = \mathrm{absLogHeight}(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,v) + \mathrm{absLogHeight}(\mathrm{evalVec}\,s\,w) - \mathrm{absLogHeight}(\mathrm{chordVec}\,s\,v\,w)$. The assertion is that there exists a real constant $C \ge 0$ such that $-C \le \mathrm{pairHt}\,s\,v\,w$ for all places $v, w$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This is the elementary one-sided bound making the chordal pair height bounded below uniformly in the two places, the quantitative input ensuring that the height form built from pair heights is bounded below. It is used for the analogous lower bound for the base height [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_forall_neg_le_baseHt`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_forall_neg_le_baseHt) and in the estimates [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_forall_neg_le_pairHt.lean

